# Engli Everything Example
# This program demonstrates many Engli language features

# Variables and arithmetic
Set name to "Engli Programmer".
Set age to 25.
Set score to 100.
Set active to true.

Say "Hello, {name}!".
Say "Age: {age}".
Say "Score: {score}".
Say "Active: {active}".

# Arithmetic operations
Set result to (10 plus 5) multiplied by 2.
Say "Result: {result}".

# Conditionals
If age is greater than or equal to 18:

    Say "You are an adult.".

Otherwise:

    Say "You are a minor.".

# Loops
Set total to 0.

For each number from 1 through 10:

    Add number to total.

End the loop.

Say "Sum of 1-10: {total}".

# Functions
Define a function called greet that takes person:

    Say "Hello, {person}!".

End the function.

greet with "World".

# Recursion
Define a function called factorial that takes n:

    If n is less than or equal to 1:

        Return 1.

    Return n multiplied by factorial with n minus 1.

End the function.

Say "5! = {factorial with 5}".

# Lists
Set numbers to a list containing 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5.
Say "Numbers: {numbers}".
Say "First number: {numbers at index 0}".

Add 6 to numbers.
Say "After adding 6: {numbers}".

# Maps
Set person to a map containing:
    "name" mapped to "AB",
    "age" mapped to 25.

Say "Person name: {person at \"name\"}".
Say "Person age: {person at \"age\"}".

# Objects
Create an object called player.
Set player.name to "Hero".
Set player.health to 100.
Say "Player: {player.name}, Health: {player.health}".

# Custom types
Define a type called Player:
    A Player has a name which is text.
    A Player has health which is a number.
End the type.

Set hero to a Player with:
    name equal to "Hero",
    health equal to 100.

# Enums
Define an enumeration called Direction containing:
    North,
    South,
    East,
    West.
End the enumeration.

Set direction to Direction.North.

# Pattern matching
Match direction:
    When direction is Direction.North:
        Say "Going North".
    When direction is Direction.South:
        Say "Going South".
    Otherwise:
        Say "Other direction".
End the match.

# Time
Set now to the current date and time.
Say "Current time: {now}".

Set timestamp to the current Unix timestamp.
Say "Unix timestamp: {timestamp}".

# Random
Set random_num to a random number between 1 and 100.
Say "Random number: {random_num}".

# Error handling
Try:

    Set x to 10 divided by 0.

If an error occurs as error:

    Say "Error caught: {error.message}".

# File operations
Write "Hello from Engli!" to the file "test_output.txt".

Read the file "test_output.txt" into contents.
Say "File contents: {contents}".

If the file "test_output.txt" exists:

    Say "File exists!".

Delete the file "test_output.txt".

# Environment variables
Get the environment variable "HOME" and store it in home.
Say "Home directory: {home}".

# Terminal commands
Run the command "echo"
with arguments "Hello from terminal"
and store the result in result.

Say "Terminal output: {result.output}".

Say "Engli program completed successfully!".
